      "op": "spawn",
      "role": "builder",
      "task": "Write module.py and test_cases.json. module.py: solve(data) per user contract. Process data['ops'] in order without mutating input. State: balance=0, holds dict id->amount. For each op, in order: (1) kind must be one of credit, debit, hold, release else ValueError (also ValueError if op is not a dict). (2) for credit/debit/hold, amount must be int (not bool) and >=1 else ValueError. (3) hold: id must not already be an active hold; release: id must be an active hold; else ValueError. (4) debit/hold: amount must not exceed available = balance - sum(holds) else ValueError. credit adds balance; debit subtracts; hold adds holds[id]=amount; release deletes holds[id], ignoring amount. Return {'balance','held','available'} ints; empty ops returns zeros. Standard library only, no I/O. test_cases.json: JSON list of at least 8 distinct cases, each with 'input' and exactly one of 'output' or 'error' (exception class name, e.g. ValueError). Cover: empty ops, credit+debit, hold reducing available, release freeing funds and ignoring amount, duplicate hold id error, release unknown id error, debit exceeding available (due to hold) error, bool amount error, amount 0 error, unknown kind error, ordering (invalid amount checked before unknown id for release is N/A; e.g. hold with amount 0 and duplicate id raises ValueError). Expectations must match the contract exactly."
